  string back into that shape. One concept, two representations.                                                                                                
  3. Speculative Generality (redundant declaration) — state.ts:18  "x-state"?: unknown;  in  StateSchema extends JsonSchema .  JsonSchema  already opens        
  with  [k: string]: unknown  (state.ts:15), so the redeclaration adds no type information. Harmless intent marker, but it declares nothing tsc uses.           
  4. Tautological test (tdd skill) — state.test.ts:69  expect(loaded.params).toEqual(DEFAULT_PARAMS);  asserts output equals the module's own exported          
  constant, so it passes by construction. state.test.ts:70 already supplies the independent literal, so line 69 is the "recomputes the expected value the       
  way the code does" anti-pattern.                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                
